A||||8||Mach10||Door alignment problems?||||10||
Z||000000||Mach10||10-16-2001||01:27 AM||||I've run the search, but haven't been able to find quite what I need:<P>My door closes ok, it's just that it's not 100% lined-up to the striker pin. Yank the handle, and it kinda grates off it. Looks fine, so I'm figuring it's out by only a degree or two. What's the easiest, fastest way of adjusting this? The door seems to hang maybe 1-2mm too low. Still closes OK, just not terribly smoothly...<P>I'm wondering if this might be related to this odd bump I have on the driver's floor. There's no evidence of an accident (panels line up, visual insp. of frame members show no problems. Can't help but wonder if the first owner (who, as I look over the car more and more, appears to have beaten on the poor thing) hadn't hit a really bad pothole and bent something. The car runs straight, handles fine. Underneath, I can't see any damage/bending. Don't know wtf is up with this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||SLYGUY||10-16-2001||02:14 AM||||I hear ya on that one. <BR>The previous owner of my GT was the original, but he let it go in the end also. <BR>The moulding on the lowest portion of the door is cooked on the passenger side. I went over it with a magnifying glass and there doesn't seem to be any evidence of an accident. What is the best way to remove that and how would I replace it after I straighten it?<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||10-16-2001||02:15 AM||||LOL!!<P>It's not "cooked", its CROOKED!!<P>LMDAO!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||10-16-2001||06:56 AM||||Mach 10<BR>You can adjust the striker pin a little bit.  If there is noticeable up and down movement in the door, I'd say change the hinge pins.  The doors are heavy and if they're original, it's probably due.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I have a different pass door and figured it got a minor bump at some time.  I took the pass seat out the other day and it assumed a pretzel shape so maybe it wasn't so minor.  Seems to drive Okay, tho.<P>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||10-16-2001||07:29 AM||||the striker pin is in an enlarged hole so you can loosen it slightly and move it all around. If the door is hanging down, you can adjust it by loosening the mounting bolts on hinges. BEWARE-TINY ADJUSTMENTS HAVE LARGE EFFECT, so do it a little at a time.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||10-16-2001||10:01 AM||||Well, the door's not loose on the hinges. It swings nicely. It's just out of alignment  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Thanks! I just now have to find the hoarking-big torx bit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'm going to crawl under the car and see if I can't find a dent of something. If I do, I'm going to eventually pull the carpetting out, and flatten that bump with a sledge-hammer and a body pusher. &gt;:\||||reg||10
Z||000006||Captain Midnight||10-17-2001||02:59 AM||||I loosened my hinge bolts, but the door would not adjust. Is it supose to move?<P>------------------<BR>Captain Midnight||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||10-17-2001||10:33 AM||||yes supposed to move like a 1/4 inch in any direction. If its never been moved before the sealer may have it stuck. loosen the 4 bolts more and use a screwdriver or pry bar to loosen it. You will prob need a floor jack or helping hand to help you hold the door when your adjusting it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rick 88||10-17-2001||06:18 PM||||My hinge pins do not have any up and down movement but there is some wear on the striker pins. Especially on the drivers door since it gets more use. I would like to replace them. Are the pins the same as on other GM cars.<P>Rick 88||||reg||5
